      "message": "1) Sure, I can change to only revert the MAX_DRM_OPEN_COUNT part in drm_file.c.\n\n2) In gfxstream Vulkan driver, we will open one fd for every host visible vkAllocateMemory(and we will try to reuse opened fd if that memory is vkFreeMemory\u0027ed), I am not sure if we could decide a reasonable limit for that. We can use a different way to manage the mapped memory: use the drm gem object instead of a rendernode fd to manage the underlying resources(see https://r.android.com/1836503), but the AEMU team thinks that removing the limit in the kernel is an easier fix. WDYT?",
